From 3cef2316438431cb666217184b3120ac9e48d528 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:07:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Move the coven pin and the checker to coven 9e92d464d

coven now keeps coven_pending as a table app triggers can follow, reads its
named view columns as its own types, and builds the checker's owner graph
once. It moved to rusqlite 0.42, so bae's rusqlite and libsqlite3-sys move
with it.

A coven live query no longer has an async next(): an async reader awaits
changed() and runs run_changed() on a blocking thread. LiveResults in
bae-store does that for every async reader in bae, and keeps a run's result
for the next read when its reader stopped waiting, so a select! loses
nothing. Tests on an async executor read with coven's next_inline().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
